#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0410 expect=noViolation domain=SV
#note "Authority: SDTM/SDTMIG Conformance Rules v2.0 CG0410, Condition 'Scheduled or Contingent visit (exists in TV)', Rule 'VISITNUM identifies unique record within subject'. THE S3 FOREIGN-DISCRIMINATION PIN (SKELETON-distinct-function hazard 3), which for this rule can only be a noViolation because the Check tests 'VISITNUM in $tv_visitnum'. Subject S1-001 has two records with the UNPLANNED, non-integral VISITNUM 1.5 (rows 2 and 3). 1.5 is not in TV, so the Condition (scheduled or contingent visit, i.e. exists in TV) does not hold and CG0410 says nothing -> silent. Every planned VISITNUM is unique within subject. A port that read VISITNUM from the primary SV instead of TV would find 1.5 in its own set, and the duplicate would FIRE. Also the numeric pin: VISITNUM is Num on both sides and the discriminating value is non-integral."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset SV label="Subject Visits"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
col SVSTDTC  type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Visit"
---
S1 | SV | S1-001 | 1   | SCREENING       | 2024-01-02
S1 | SV | S1-001 | 1.5 | UNSCHEDULED 1.5 | 2024-01-05
S1 | SV | S1-001 | 1.5 | UNSCHEDULED 1.5 | 2024-01-07
S1 | SV | S1-001 | 2   | BASELINE        | 2024-01-10
---

dataset TV label="Trial Visits"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
col TVSTRL   type=Char label="Visit Start Rule"
---
S1 | TV | 1 | SCREENING | Start of screening
S1 | TV | 2 | BASELINE  | Day 1
S1 | TV | 3 | WEEK 4    | Day 29
---
